# What an ecosystem adapter answers: what it recognizes of its tool in a directory, the exact versions of what that asks,
# and the settings files that tool needs in a task. An adapter opens a connection in Resolve alone and nowhere else,
# never runs the project's code, and holds no credential.
# Every field is required and of its declared type, an int being whole: an answer with one missing or of another type is
# refused, never read as empty or false.
interface org.fuin.porelo.Ecosystem1

# Which ecosystem, the name its executable is installed under, and the version of this contract it was built against.
method Describe() -> (protocolVersion: int, ecosystem: string)

# One value an adapter recognized. part says what it belongs to; file and line where it is set, line 0 when the file has
# no line for it. origin says who wrote it: YOURS the person, file relative to the home; CHECKOUT the checkout, file
# relative to the directory; MACHINE neither, such as a parent in a local repository or the tool's built-in default, file
# relative to the home, absolute when it lies outside the home, or "" with line 0 when the value comes from no file. Only
# MACHINE may have no file or an absolute one, and no file holds "..". unknown says
# the key is set where it cannot be read without running something; value is then "", and refused otherwise. A
# credential is named by its id only: never its value.
type Finding (
    part: (TOOLS, RULES),
    key: string,
    value: string,
    file: string,
    line: int,
    origin: (YOURS, CHECKOUT, MACHINE),
    unknown: bool,
    note: string
)

# Something an adapter read and can place in no part: where it is, and what it is. A file that keeps the adapter from
# trusting what it read of the checkout is reported here, naming that file, with a note. Never a credential's value.
type Unplaced (file: string, line: int, note: string)

# What the adapter recognizes of its tool in a directory, and in the files of the home the person's own settings are in.
# It reads them and writes nothing.
method Detect(directory: string, home: string) -> (findings: []Finding, unplaced: []Unplaced)

# Looks up, once, what Detect read: called only when a project file is made, never for a start with a file. findings are
# this adapter's own Detect findings for the directory and home, and no other adapter's. The answer replaces them whole.
# Two kinds of key are placed by their prefix alone: run.<name>, Containerfile lines for the image, RUN, ARG and ENV only
# and a COPY from an image pinned by its digest, joined in the order of the names; and env.<NAME>, a variable's value for the image. A name Porelo sets in every task,
# PATH among them, is refused. This is the one method that may open a connection: the adapter is started for it with
# HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY and their lower-case forms where the person has them set, and nothing else. It
# keeps each request within 5 seconds, and Porelo waits 20 seconds for the whole answer; a value it cannot look up in
# time is unknown. A proxy setting never goes into an answer. An adapter that cannot say answers
# org.varlink.service.MethodNotFound, and what Detect found stands.
method Resolve(directory: string, home: string, findings: []Finding) -> (findings: []Finding)

# A repository a task's tool reaches: its name and its URL inside the task.
type Repository (name: string, url: string)

# A settings file for the task. path is relative to the task user's home: names joined by single slashes, none blank,
# "." or "..", with no quote, backslash or control character. ownerOnly says whether only that user may read it.
type File (path: string, content: string, ownerOnly: bool)

# The files the tool's settings need so that it reaches these repositories. Given no directory, since nothing reads a
# task's workspace from the host, it answers whenever a repository is declared, and it writes nothing itself.
# extension is what the project keeps for this adapter alone, unread by Porelo and absent when it keeps nothing: plain
# JSON values, at most 16384 bytes as compact JSON and 8 levels deep. It never widens what a task reaches.
method Configure(repositories: []Repository, extension: ?object) -> (files: []File)

# The directory holds nothing of this adapter's tool.
error NotRecognized ()

# A file it needs cannot be read: detail says which and why, never what the file holds.
error Unreadable (detail: string)
